<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy July jet fuel.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy July jet fuel.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy jet fuel for July 1-30 delivery, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on May 22 and offers are valid to May 23.</p>
<p>The official to Reuters earlier that Taiwan did not issue any tender to buy jet fuel for June delivery due to ample inventory.</p>
<p>CPC generally imports one or two 32,000 tonne cargoes jet fuel a month.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought one cargo for May 21-30 delivery at $204 per tonne on a cost-and-freight basis to Keelung or Shen Ao.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3093)</p>
